#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129211 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92cc3d27-0e31-571f-9b92-4f209c5a08e0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c5c064b-08ea-5bfd-ab69-59d08747b4f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278982} {:answer/id #uuid "36add068-fc21-5310-b6d6-2c342cf02faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279070} {:answer/id #uuid "402db993-f88f-5fbe-94b2-191a8a4097a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279160} {:answer/id #uuid "a97f6f5d-dae7-50c8-b1bc-6c5e4d06a4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280096} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6093ca-d163-58ee-a9e0-b840646a5e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf6093ca-d163-58ee-a9e0-b840646a5e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280274} :answer-field/id #uuid "8415b494-bfb5-5759-9d5d-906937712b89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5a597a5-f786-5891-91b3-c78b73413f55" :question/math-academy-id "q-162905" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $\\frac{5M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281625 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129212 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fdc1a2a-8a35-59f2-9890-5b835693df4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30491144-e2a9-5de8-a3cd-11a0f89cc6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279013} {:answer/id #uuid "874e8595-292b-5f4e-bd66-51a639f6022f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279801} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6b9256-f496-53ff-aad8-44a1442bdf5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279983} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9e4de9-d138-53fa-bcae-346a8056acc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280250} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a5a940-b3ec-59b0-9c37-09b3fc4d604e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "874e8595-292b-5f4e-bd66-51a639f6022f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279801} :answer-field/id #uuid "07946d72-168a-58f9-99a2-0417d27cc3e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c204945d-1cc7-5037-a46b-3df54b66b209" :question/math-academy-id "q-163183" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dc61efd6e5ef1fd46fca53f7c1e47394c6b9c95fb2455dc0c798d9936a68631b.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $x$-axis, $y$-axis, and the curve $y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. If the mass density function of $D$ is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=10y,$ find the moment of inertia of the lamina about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/62/626cbf8e182d9eebb8b48026f07c5dd012c1096cc9568465f3648710ea0d07a4.png)\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(10y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}10{x}^{2}y+10{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5{x}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})+\\frac{5}{2}{(4-{x}^{2})}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{2}(4-{x}^{2})(2{x}^{2}+4-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}16-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{[16x-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(32-\\frac{32}{5}) \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281632 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129211 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92cc3d27-0e31-571f-9b92-4f209c5a08e0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35a4e499-61e4-5d51-8488-e60716c8b89c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279063} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc2f52c-6937-5664-b1ad-a8e9f01fba53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279296} {:answer/id #uuid "77349270-7aa3-5ac9-a411-62c1c99df8b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279656} {:answer/id #uuid "81467cbe-f5a5-5724-8a67-a32eb23c17bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3M}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279753} {:answer/id #uuid "e207c367-c309-58d1-92c5-7517420bb1d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77349270-7aa3-5ac9-a411-62c1c99df8b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279656} :answer-field/id #uuid "5beaea88-1fc4-552a-a4a5-3b0f75db282a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4167aa80-a0c6-5dcf-ad5c-868018ed4d84" :question/math-academy-id "q-163201" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 3=6.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}[x]_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $3M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129211 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92cc3d27-0e31-571f-9b92-4f209c5a08e0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c84deba-cb38-5f3b-af0e-58521ec502a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279280} {:answer/id #uuid "a25defa0-44b9-5bda-a10f-e6ef6a677aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280035} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5bf3b6-9c4b-50ce-879e-8ec79739fdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280127} {:answer/id #uuid "ca352098-298f-5e14-a7d7-0c7272084e0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280364} {:answer/id #uuid "cf1d4484-aff6-5376-8a09-a8cd9f6af638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5bf3b6-9c4b-50ce-879e-8ec79739fdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280127} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a384dc8-494e-5973-bebc-5b4d13e8a8c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "095d8c09-ff9b-5528-8c3d-3967d18698a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163204" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{[\\frac{8y}{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}(3-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $\\frac{4M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281642 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eba1f811-7b7d-56f6-8b49-4e7a4c7db81b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Moments of Inertia Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17226919-ce93-5049-994f-31d7cd5c10fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278798} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3b17cc-de83-57bb-914f-013137289a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279586} {:answer/id #uuid "78cff65f-0d69-5e60-9e1c-47253821dc1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279669} {:answer/id #uuid "8d83c82c-bb2f-532f-ab7d-a58f6e2cc4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279853} {:answer/id #uuid "e875a915-69ff-5a94-9c30-f7fd03b5fb84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d3b17cc-de83-57bb-914f-013137289a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279586} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf0fe541-fc86-58e2-a9d5-645ba6b20816" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2726afac-54d3-5734-a6e0-8fa5ce77d367" :question/math-academy-id "q-163228" :question/problem "![](images/04/044395de3b30755d0c83d489709c38420827f6984af740bc56a3dc5bfaa33794.png)\n\nConsider the plate that occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the polar circles $r=2$ and $r=3$ and the polar rays $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that the region $D$ in polar coordinates can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,2\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nAlso, the mass density function in polar coordinates is \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({\\int }_{2}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{3}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-4)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
